Slot 087 is spent, not free.

087_tool_artifacts.sql shipped in 0.57.0. Besides two columns, three
functions and the analysis_reports table it created the `tool_activity`
view with `CREATE VIEW … FROM tool_call_ledger`, and `tool_call_ledger` is a
core declarative view the installer only creates after every migration has
run. On a database that had never booted on core >= 0.55 the migration
failed at "relation tool_call_ledger does not exist" — the 0.52.0 rung of
the schema-upgrade ladder reproduces it. The view is declarative
(schema/46_tool_artifacts.sql); everything else moved verbatim to
089_tool_artifacts_without_view.sql. Databases that applied 087 keep their
tracking row and 089 is a no-op for them.

Numbering continues at the highest slot ever used, never at the first gap.
